{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Symbol","language":"Translingual","definitions":[{"definition":"<i><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO%20639-5\" class=\"extiw\">ISO 639-5</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/language_code\">language code</a> for </i><b>Formosan languages</b><i>.</i>"}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":""},{"definition":"A small-to-medium-sized canine <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/mammal\" title=\"mammal\">mammal</a>, related to dogs and wolves, of the following groups:\n<ol><li>Any member of the genus <span class=\"biota\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Vulpes#Translingual\"><i>Vulpes</i></a></span>.<link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:X\">\n\n<ol><li class=\"senseid\" id=\"English:_Q8331\"> The red fox.</li></ol></li></ol>","examples":["The quick brown <b>fox</b> jumps over the lazy dog."]},{"definition":"Any member of the genus <span class=\"biota\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Vulpes#Translingual\" title=\"Vulpes\"><i>Vulpes</i></a></span>; a true fox.\n\n<ol><li class=\"senseid\"> The red fox.</li></ol>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\"></span> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/red_fox\">red fox</a>, a small carnivore (<i>Vulpes vulpes</i>) with red or silver fur."},{"definition":"The fur of a fox."},{"definition":"A fox terrier."},{"definition":"A cunning person."},{"definition":"Seventh definition, not shown."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Verb","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"To trick, fool or outwit (someone) by cunning or ingenuity."}]}],"fr":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"French","definitions":[{"definition":"Un mot français d’essai."}]}]}
